":"FL","zipCode":"33199","country":"USA"},"grass":true,"images":[]},"attendance":8230},"article":{"headline":"Brown and Bourgeois power Middle Tennessee past Florida International 26-23","description":"— Terrence Brown rushed for 158 yards and a touchdown, and Dominic Bourgeois made four field goals as Middle Tennessee held off Florida International 26-23 on Tuesday night.","story":"MIAMI -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5306988/terrence-brown\" target=\"_new\">Terrence Brown</a> rushed for 158 yards and a touchdown, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5383060/dominic-bourgeois\" target=\"_new\">Dominic Bourgeois</a> made four field goals as Middle Tennessee held off Florida International 26-23 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Blue Raiders (4-3, 2-1 Conference USA) trailed 8-7 after the first quarter before Bourgeois made field goals of 51 and 39 yards for a 13-8 halftime lead.\n\n\r\n              Bourgeois added a 50-yard field goal in the third before FIU tied the game at 16 on JJ Kohl’s 1-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4698120/kevin-schaeffer\" target=\"_new\">Kevin Schaeffer</a> and Devonte Lyons’ 2-point conversion.\n\n\r\n              Brown answered with a 54-yard touchdown run with 2:06 left in the third to put Middle Tennessee back in front for good at 23-16.\n\n\r\n              Bourgeois tacked on a 28-yard field goal early in the fourth to extend the lead to 26-16.\n\n\r\n              FIU (3-3, 1-1) pulled within three when Kohl connected with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5164324/sterling-joseph\" target=\"_new\">Sterling Joseph</a> for a 21-yard touchdown with 6:06 remaining. But Middle Tennessee chewed up the rest of the clock on an 11-play, 71-yard drive. \n\n\r\n              Brown averaged 8.8 yards on 18 carries. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5194626/roman-gagliano\" target=\"_new\">Roman Gagliano</a> threw for 200 yards and a touchdown and added 41 yards rushing for Middle Tennessee.\n\n\r\n              Kohl threw for 179 yards and three touchdowns, while Lyons rushed for 115 yards.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Middle Tennessee: Hosts Kennesaw State on Oct. 28\n\n\r\n              Florida International: At Liberty on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-21T02:50:07Z"}}